      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 8789cd12ec033b821b117446bc9edcf945cbdee1\nparent 8815bc64653ffa12d528a261fddbf7af2ff001e1\nauthor Jorge Espada <jorge@esprim.io> 1793361406 -0300\ncommitter fanquake <fanquake@gmail.com> 1795638824 +0000\n\nguix: compute --build triplet when lowering, not at load time\n\nbuilding-on read %current-system when manifest_build.scm was loaded. guix\nshell loads the manifest before it applies --system, so a\n--system=aarch64-linux build on an x86_64 machine configured the aarch64\ntoolchain with --build=x86_64-guix-linux-gnu, and gcc-cross failed to\nconfigure. Make building-on a procedure so each derivation uses its own\nsystem. Native builds produce the same derivations as before.\n\nGithub-Pull: #36709\nRebased-From: d7a8360f4ef5ff90b71d87b15ec4c5048b9ea0a9\n",
